          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చేదు (cēdu) — \"bitter, bitterness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చేదు (cēdu) is bitterness — neem leaf, some greens, most medicine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is inherited, and Telugu does not treat it as a fault. Bitter is eaten deliberately at the opening of the year and at the opening of a meal, on the understanding that it does you good."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It carries over into speech unchanged. చేదు (cēdu) news is bad news, and a చేదు (cēdu) truth is one you are told anyway."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three. The one eaten on purpose."
            }
          ]
        },
