          "title": "You'll want to know: కారం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కారం (kāraṁ) — \"pungency, heat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కారం (kāraṁ) is heat — the bite of మిరప, and by an easy extension the chilli powder itself."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ask for something with తక్కువ కారం (kāraṁ) and you will be understood anywhere, though in one or two households you will be heard as having said something mildly insulting."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is inherited. Do not read it into the end of నమస్కారం, which is a different word altogether, Sanskrit, and means a making."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. And the one you may want తక్కువ of."
            }
          ]
        },
